  "tooltip.simpleblocks.collapsed.1": "So dense it slows you down in your inventory.",
  "tooltip.simpleblocks.collapsed.2": "1 stack: Slowness I, 2: II, 9: III.",
  "item.simpleblocks.guide_book": "Simple Blocks Guide",
  "simpleblocks.guide.chapter": "Simple Blocks",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.1.title": "Simple Blocks",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.1": "The missing building blocks: Hushed Deepslate Tiles that swallow vibrations like wool, Sculk Deepslate,",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.2.title": "Simple Blocks",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.2": "the missing Vanilla stairs, slabs and walls, cracked and mossy bricks and the Shapecutter, which cuts stone and wood.",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.3.title": "Shapecutter",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.3": "The Vanilla stonecutter on a polished iron base with copper corner caps and a polished steel blade, for stone AND wood:",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.4.title": "Shapecutter",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.4": "it cuts everything the stonecutter cuts, plus planks, logs, wool and every other block whose stairs or slabs the stonecutter cannot make.",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.5.title": "Hushed Deepslate Tiles",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.5": "Deepslate tiles that swallow vibrations like wool: a Sculk Sensor or Warden does not hear a vibration that passes through the block, and walking on it makes none.",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.6.title": "Sculk Deepslate",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.6": "Deepslate with sculk veins. It is not generated in the world: craft it or find it in Ancient City chests.",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.7.title": "Sculk Tiles",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.7": "Deepslate tiles in sculk colors: each tile a little lighter or darker, a few sculk sparks breathe slowly.",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.8.title": "Missing Stairs, Slabs and Walls",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.8": "Stairs, slabs and walls Vanilla lacks: Calcite, Netherrack and Smooth Basalt (all three), Cut (Red) Sandstone stairs and walls, Smooth (Red) Sandstone walls. Since the palette completion (IG31-42):",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.9.title": "Missing Stairs, Slabs and Walls",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.9": "stairs, slabs and walls for the mossy bricks, End Stone,",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.10.title": "Missing Stairs, Slabs and Walls",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.10": "Quartz Bricks and the missing walls and stairs of Stone, Polished Granite/Diorite/Andesite, Quartz, Smooth Quartz, Purpur, Prismarine Bricks and",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.11.title": "Missing Stairs, Slabs and Walls",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.11": "Dark Prismarine.",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.12.title": "Cracked and Mossy Bricks",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.12": "Aged variants of Vanilla bricks that have none:",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.13.title": "Cracked and Mossy Bricks",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.13": "cracked Red Nether, Tuff, Mud, End Stone, Cinnabar and Sulfur bricks; mossy Tuff, Mud, End Stone, Cinnabar and Sulfur bricks, mossy Deepslate Bricks and Tiles.",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.14.title": "Cracked and Mossy Bricks",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.14": "Also cracked Prismarine, Prismarine Bricks, Dark Prismarine, Polished Deepslate and Blue Nether Bricks (smelt the base block).",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.15.title": "Blue Nether Bricks",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.15": "A blue counterpart to Red Nether Bricks, with stairs, slab and wall.",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.16.title": "Natural Block Variants",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.16": "Slabs of dirt, grass, sand and gravel, chiseled packed and blue ice, cracked ice, a nautilus shell block and froglights in three more colors.",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.17.title": "Suspended and Levitating Sand and Gravel",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.17": "Sand and gravel without gravity (suspended) and with reversed gravity (levitating).",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.18.title": "Snowlogging",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.18": "Use a snow layer on a fence, a small flower, grass, a fern or a bush and the snow shares the block with it, like in Bedrock Edition: the plant or fence stays visible in the snow.",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.19.title": "Frost Grass",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.19": "A grass block with snow on top slowly freezes to Frost Grass in cold biomes or with ice below it; without snow it slowly thaws back to grass.",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.20.title": "Pale Blocks",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.20": "A pumpkin, carved pumpkin, jack o'lantern, melon or hay bale placed in the Pale Garden slowly fades like copper weathers: Faded, then Bleached, then Pale (the end stage). Use a honeycomb on it to keep it as it is (Waxed);",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.21.title": "Pale Blocks",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.21": "an axe takes the wax off or scrapes one stage back.",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.22.title": "Compressed, Dense and Collapsed blocks",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.22": "Stage 1 Compressed = 9 blocks, stage 2 Dense = 9 Compressed, stage 3 Collapsed = 9 Dense, for 19 common Vanilla building blocks (dirt, mud, cobblestone, stone, sand, red sand, gravel, clay,",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.23.title": "Compressed, Dense and Collapsed blocks",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.23": "netherrack, cobbled deepslate, andesite, diorite, granite, tuff, sandstone, red sandstone, end stone, blackstone, soul sand).",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.24.title": "Settings",
  "simpleblocks.guide.page.24": "More settings are in the mod's config screen.",
